ts/freedimensional/on-the-move-report/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/freedimensional/on-the-move-report/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Open Engagement w/ Sunview + Amber Art</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/31-open-engagement/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/31-open-engagement/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Operação Macabéa</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/luv-til-it-hurts/operacao-macabea/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/luv-til-it-hurts/operacao-macabea/</guid><description/></item><item><title>PAIM calendar</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/27-paim-calendar/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/27-paim-calendar/</guid><description/></item><item><title>pARTage exhibition: Global Warming (Mauritius)</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/farm-school/partage/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/farm-school/partage/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Partnership w/ Humans as Hosts</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/luv-til-it-hurts/humans-as-hosts/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/luv-til-it-hurts/humans-as-hosts/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Princeton visit</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/33-princeton-tour/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/33-princeton-tour/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Publication Studio: São Paulo</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/11-pssp/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/11-pssp/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Rádio Santos Dvmont</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/15-fugitive-radio/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/15-fugitive-radio/</guid><description/></item><item><title>SARAI Reader #9: projections</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/10-sarai-pdf/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/10-sarai-pdf/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Steinvorth research: emerging cultural structures</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/05-sofias-youtube/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/05-sofias-youtube/</guid><description/></item><item><title>summary</title><link>https://tllester.info/projects/el-mejor-karate/summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/projects/el-mejor-karate/summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Once an esteemed writer asked me if I’m a spy, sitting at Veselka. The title of a cool teacher’s book, &lt;em&gt;I Want to Show You More&lt;/em&gt; is also befitting. EMK is the advance-planner of a work; anything spied upon is first seen as the makings of a story. Sometimes I read from the story at an open-mic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EMK is a name I’ve made for myself whose backstory spans NYC, Mexico City, Cairo, São Paulo and Tennessee. It started as minor graffiti–stickers–co-designed with artist friends: Adham Bakry (Egypt), Gustavo Marcasse (Brazil), and Jakub Szczęsny (Poland). Besides sticking stickers, EMK writes and performs interventions.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>summary</title><link>https://tllester.info/projects/farm-school/summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/projects/farm-school/summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;FARM/SCHOOL began to take shape in 2020 regarding a farm parcel in Middle Tennessee where I grew up. It takes on–and plays with–both theme and time differently than the 20-year series comprised of freeDimensional, Lanchonete(.)org &amp;amp; Luv ‘til it Hurts, while benefitting from its field of methods and lessons learned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FARM/SCHOOL is the name of a proposed artist residency under development. Within its framework, the initials &amp;lsquo;f/s&amp;rsquo; reflect the process of homecoming / going, something I write about.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>summary</title><link>https://tllester.info/projects/freedimensional/summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/projects/freedimensional/summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A 10 year project (2003-12), fD urged a sea change in the artist residency sector by practicing artist shelter and evacuation placements, convening networks and coalitions of expert practice, and sharing lessons learned in immigration and cultural policy fora.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After 10 years, fD changed its name to ArtistSafety(.)net in order to maintain ongoing projects in partnership with other artists and organizations, e.g. Sidd Joag, Mary Ann DeVlieg, Artistic Freedom Initiative, Residency Unlimited, Hildesheim University and the Westbeth Artists Community.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>summary</title><link>https://tllester.info/projects/lanchonete/summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/projects/lanchonete/summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;From 2013 to 2018 a group of artists called our interventions on the right to the city in the center of São Paulo by the project name, Lanchonete(.)org. Along the way we acquired a small bar on a denigrated yet swiftly gentrifying street in the center of São Paulo as nucleus for artist and urbanist residencies, community meals, open courses, concerts, murals, public health campaigns and a radio station.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lanchonete(.)org welcomed 100 residents over five years. It began as an idea with Raphael Daibert and grew to include a rotating cast of local artists and activists including Paula Querido Van Erven, Lorena Vicini, MARGEM, Laura Davina, Daniel Lühmann, Joel Borges, BAIXO CENTRO, Cidades Sem Fome, Ocupação São João, Gabriela Baraúna, Isabel Gandia, Thiago Gonçalves, Rodrigo Bueno, EXPLODE!, Casarão Belvedere, Marcelo Ferreira, and many others.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>summary</title><link>https://tllester.info/projects/luv-til-it-hurts/summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/projects/luv-til-it-hurts/summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;From 2018-2020, Luv ’til it Hurts engaged poz artists and allies from around the world to understand their local HIV-related stigmas and challenges. Intended as its R&amp;amp;D phase, the project developed a flexible device for deployment to the global AIDS front called Exquisite Corpse, an evolving group show, interactive game and soapbox that can be homemade and occur wherever needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LUV process and resulting Exquisite Corpse are the fruit of many artists and organizers working together, including Jakub Szczęsny, Brad Walrond, Sebastien Santamaria, Adham Bakry, Paula Nishijima, ANKH Association, Residency Unlimited, Daniel Santiago Salguero, and Love Positive Women.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>summary</title><link>https://tllester.info/projects/my-art-world/summary/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/projects/my-art-world/summary/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;NASA proudly landed a spacecraft on Mars early in Biden’s 1st term, yet throughout the history of space travel there has been no credible sighting of the art world and many haven’t even heard of it. The outcome I’ve been asked to pursue is therefore complicated not by a majority wanting confirmation the art world exists, but by one not caring whether its existence is proven or debunked, simply not knowing to care. Given that it might all be a hoax, the findings–I was told–should be useful in other arenas.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>summer school</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/farm-school/summer-school/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/farm-school/summer-school/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Tennessean op-ed</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/luv-til-it-hurts/tenessean/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/luv-til-it-hurts/tenessean/</guid><description/></item><item><title>TIJUANA book fair Lanchonete zine</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/17-lanchonete-zine/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/17-lanchonete-zine/</guid><description/></item><item><title>VACANT</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/1/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/1/</guid><description/></item><item><title>VACUOUS</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/2/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/2/</guid><description/></item><item><title>VAPID</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/3/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/3/</guid><description/></item><item><title>VOLDEMORT</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/4/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/el-mejor-karate/4/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Zona da Mata</title><link>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/12-zonadamata/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tllester.info/posts/lanchonete/12-zonadamata/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>